Q: Get unlimited row count and paginated results from the database using CodeIgniter A: <p>To avoid writing most of the query builder calls in two separate places, some CodeIgniter developers opt to build the shared clauses, then call <code>count_all_results()</code> and use its second parameter to explicitly NOT reset the query builder object - this way you can use it in a subsequent execution without repeating the already built clauses.</p>
<p>Because the <code>count_all_results()</code> method will build the FROM clause, your <code>get()</code> call doesn't need to re-declare the table.</p>
<p>Do not use <code>num_rows()</code> to access the row count because that query demands that the database return whole records - which you don't intend to use. Execute a COUNT() query with <code>count_all_results()</code>.</p>
<p>The call site for the following method should be written to access the dyadic, associative array returned.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function getTotalRowsAndLimitedResults(int $id, ?int $limit = null, ?int $offset = null): array
{
    $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;join($this-&gt;db-&gt;dbprefix . 'page p', 'p.page_id = p2c.page_id', 'left')
        -&gt;join($this-&gt;db-&gt;dbprefix . 'page_description pd', 'pd.page_id = p2c.page_id', 'left')
        -&gt;or_where([
            'p2c.parent_id' =&gt; $id,
            'p2c.category_id' =&gt; $id,
         ]);

    return [
        'total' =&gt; $this-&gt;db-&gt;count_all_results($this-&gt;db-&gt;dbprefix . 'page_to_category p2c', false),
        'result' =&gt; $this-&gt;db-&gt;get('', $limit, $offset)-&gt;result_array(),
    ];
}
</code></pre>

Q: How can I convert a string to integer in C? A: <p>In C++, you can use such a function:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>template &lt;typename T&gt;
T to(const std::string &amp; s)
{
    std::istringstream stm(s);
    T result;
    stm &gt;&gt; result;

    if(stm.tellg() != s.size())
        throw error;

    return result;
}
</code></pre>
<p>This can help you to convert any string to any type such, as float, int, double, etc.</p>
